# Copy to `.env`. Every value here is optional — the app builds, runs, and
# passes its e2e suite with none of them set. Nothing in `.env` is ever
# committed (see .gitignore).
#
# What does NOT belong here: Apple notary credentials. Those live in
# ~/.config/apple-notary.env under ONLOOK_-prefixed names, are sourced by the
# shell, and are mapped into the build by scripts/cut-dmg.ts alone. Keeping them
# out of the repo's env file is what stops another project's toolchain from
# signing with Onlook's Apple account.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Telemetry
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No env needed: a write-only ingestion token is checked in
# (`PROD_POSTHOG_KEY` in apps/studio/src/main/telemetry/index.ts). It is public
# by design and can only write events. A packaged official build sends to it by
# default; a source build, a dev run included, sends to it once the person
# accepts the consent screen, unless a key override below names another
# project. An unpackaged official run sends nothing.
#
# Build-time override, wins over the checked-in token (electron-vite inlines
# MAIN_VITE_-prefixed values from this file into the main bundle). For cutting
# a build against a different project.
# MAIN_VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=
#
# Never put a personal API key for the analytics service anywhere here. It
# would ship in the DMG.

# Runtime override, wins over the baked value. For pointing a local build at a
# throwaway project without rebuilding.
# STUDIO_POSTHOG_KEY=

# Defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com
# STUDIO_POSTHOG_HOST=

# Hard off, even with a key present.
# STUDIO_TELEMETRY=0

# A never-shown (AGENT_HEADLESS) launch emits nothing unless this is set — the
# door an agent uses to prove an event landed. STUDIO_TELEMETRY=0 still wins.
# STUDIO_TELEMETRY_HEADLESS=1

# The log file, the outbox and the error owners: apps/studio/src/main/{log,telemetry,errors}/.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Auto-update
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Disables the update check. A source build never updates itself and an
# unpackaged build skips the check, so this only matters for a packaged build
# whose provider has the `updates` capability.
# STUDIO_AUTO_UPDATE=0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Alternative notarization path for scripts/cut-dmg.ts: a stored notarytool
# keychain profile instead of credentials in the environment. No secret enters
# any process's env at all. Create one with:
#   xcrun notarytool store-credentials <name> --apple-id <id> --team-id <team>
# APPLE_NOTARY_KEYCHAIN_PROFILE=
